WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.420
Marcus has earned his license.

2
00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.320
Keeping it active now requires a calendar, accurate records and timely

3
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:11.400
action. Maryland producer licenses are generally renewed

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.980
every two years. An individual's expiration
is tied to the end of the birth month.

6
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.460
Renewal requires the appropriate application, fees and qualifications.

7
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.000
Continuing education has an earlier deadline.

8
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.260
Do not wait until the last day of the license to

9
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.620
begin a course. A missed email is especially dangerous if the

10
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.560
producer never updated the address held by the Administration.

11
00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.430
For a typical Maryland resident life producer, the regular requirement is

12
00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:48.600
twenty-four approved continuing-education hours in the renewal period,

13
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.810
including at least three in ethics.

14
00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:55.610
Complete the required education no later than fifteen days before license

15
00:00:55.610 --> 00:01:00.730
expiration. Hours must satisfy the applicable licensed-line requirements.

16
00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:07.010
Special statutory reductions, exceptions and approved waivers exist,

17
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.710
so do not present the regular rule as universal.

18
00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:16.950
A nonresident can satisfy Maryland's continuing-education requirement through

19
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.030
qualifying home-state compliance and reciprocity.

20
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.800
This exam-preparation course is not being represented as approved renewal credit.

21
00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.620
An expired license is not a grace period for selling.

22
00:01:31.704 --> 00:01:36.564
Maryland prohibits insurance business until reinstatement is effective.

23
00:01:37.624 --> 00:01:41.824
For up to one year after expiration, reinstatement requires the appropriate

24
00:01:41.824 --> 00:01:46.184
application, renewal fees, a one-hundred-dollar reinstatement fee

25
00:01:46.904 --> 00:01:48.284
and proof of required education.

26
00:01:49.524 --> 00:01:54.064
An application within sixty days leads to retroactive reinstatement under the

27
00:01:54.064 --> 00:01:58.804
statute. An application later than sixty days leads to prospective

28
00:01:58.804 --> 00:02:03.344
reinstatement. That distinction does not authorize someone to keep working

29
00:02:03.344 --> 00:02:06.904
while expired and simply hope to fix the record afterward.

30
00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:12.590
A licensee must report changes in legal name, trade name, email

31
00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:15.590
address or address within thirty days.

32
00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:19.810
Filing a trade name is not the same as obtaining new

33
00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:24.650
lines of authority. There is also a separate ten-day rule for

34
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:29.550
changes to the designated business-entity contact's required information.

35
00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:34.230
Read the role named in the question before choosing the clock.

36
00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:38.790
Moving between states can create additional resident or nonresident

37
00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:43.870
requirements. Updating an agency website alone does not update the

38
00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:48.920
Administration's licensing record. Two reporting rules are easy to

39
00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:54.060
confuse. A covered adverse administrative action taken by another

40
00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:59.160
jurisdiction or another Maryland government unit must be reported within

41
00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.300
thirty days after final disposition.

42
00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:06.900
A covered criminal prosecution must be reported within thirty days after

43
00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.140
the initial court appearance.

44
00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.920
The criminal rule does not generally wait for a conviction.

45
00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.120
Maryland excludes misdemeanor violations of its Vehicle Law from that

46
00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:22.040
particular criminal-reporting requirement. Use the actual statute and

47
00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:26.280
required documents for the event, instead of treating every legal matter

48
00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.620
as the same deadline.

49
00:03:28.698 --> 00:03:33.958
Imagine Marcus changes his email, approaches renewal and receives notice

50
00:03:33.958 --> 00:03:35.058
of a covered proceeding.

51
00:03:36.318 --> 00:03:39.198
These create separate duties with separate starting dates.

52
00:03:40.178 --> 00:03:44.298
He updates the licensing record, completes approved education by the earlier

53
00:03:44.298 --> 00:03:48.878
deadline, submits renewal on time and reports the proceeding with the

54
00:03:48.878 --> 00:03:54.138
required records. A timely and complete renewal application can preserve the

55
00:03:54.138 --> 00:03:58.258
existing license until the Commissioner makes a final renewal decision.

56
00:03:59.298 --> 00:04:02.578
That protection is different from letting the license expire without

57
00:04:02.578 --> 00:04:07.618
applying. Identify the event, the person responsible and the

58
00:04:07.618 --> 00:04:09.038
deadline each time.
